  "description": "Designed and built for pure freestyle performance, the La Bastille is quite literally the bike that can do it all. Designed by flatland world champion, Matthias Dandois, this bike is at home with the most technical flatland riding imaginable as it is in the streets, on ramps or at the trails. A responsive 20.25\" top tube frame is perfect for mid-sized riders and is the go-to frame for younger riders on the Haro crew. The LaBastille Cassette version has a cassette rear hub for full speed ahead engagement.\nFull chromoly frame with 1-1/8\" steerer tube and mid BB shell; 20.25\" top Tube\nFull chromoly with tapered legs & internally threaded 1-piece steerer tube. 15mm offset\nHaro full chromoly 9\" rise 2-piece\nHaro Baseline stem\nHaro Baseline grips\nHaro Baseline chromoly 8 spline 19mm cranks; 165mm length\nSealed front hub and rear cassette, 36H double wall alloy rims\n25/9 gear ratio\nHaro Base line half link chain\nHaro La Mesa tires 20x2.4\" front/rear\nFlatland specific geometry featuring 19.5\" top tube, 75.5° head tube, 71° seat tube, 12.75\" chain stays",
